2|0@tf2^1440007153#cu8i6ml:Kakoriko$:It harms the economy in a way that you can control. Because you're the supplier, you decide how expensive it is. You shouldn't be able to do this, when it wasn't meant to exist in the first place. Valve made the game, Valve put the items into the economy, and the people decided the price. When you're taking something from the game and making it yourself, without the knowledge of it's existence through the now third-party (Valve) you've taken control of the market value of said item, and are *using* the economy with it. Valve, as *the creator* of the game should have the knowledge of the items existence, and the knowledge of how it came to be. It belongs to them, as it was created with their coding. Given this, you're acting like a criminal: Using the item made from somebody else's code to turn a profit of your own. Your mindset is so criminal and inconsiderate of other's well-beings that it honestly scares me.
